(Bug #82: every row of the adjudication report's table - each one a
 two-decimal value the old runtime parser landed one ulp away from its
 own literal. The report listed twelve; sweeping all one thousand
 two-decimal values from zero up to ten against their literals found
 fifty-three, thirty of them below one, so the last four rows here are
 the proof that the fix reaches past the fractional part into values
 with an integer part too.)

